    {
     "type": "concept",
     "title": "Gern: The Word English Does Not Have",
     "content": "Here is the third irregular — and the most German word in this lesson. **Gern** (GAIRN, also written **gerne**) has no English equivalent. It is a little adverb you drop next to a verb, and it means you *like doing* that verb.\n\n• **Ich trinke Kaffee.** — I drink coffee.\n• **Ich trinke gern Kaffee.** — I like drinking coffee.\n\nEnglish rebuilds the whole sentence around \"like\". German just adds one word and keeps the sentence intact. It works with any verb: **Ich lese gern** — I like reading. **Ich koche gern** — I like cooking. **Ich spiele gern Fußball** — I like playing football.\n\nAnd gern compares, irregularly, like gut and viel:\n\n• **gern → lieber → am liebsten** (GAIRN / LEE-ber / ahm LEEP-sten)\n\n**Lieber** means you prefer it; **am liebsten** means you like it most of all. Watch one person's drinks menu:\n\n• **Ich trinke gern Kaffee.** — I like drinking coffee.\n• **Ich trinke lieber Tee.** — I prefer (drinking) tea.\n• **Ich trinke am liebsten Wasser.** — Most of all, I like drinking water.\n\nSame verb, same structure — only the little word climbs. Germans use this ladder constantly: for food, music, weekend plans, everything. Learn all three steps as one unit and you can state a preference about anything you can do.",
     "visual": {
      "type": "diagram",
      "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" class=\"lesson-visual\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"55\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"36\">THE GERN LADDER</text><rect x=\"60\" y=\"130\" width=\"980\" height=\"120\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"rgba(139,92,246,0.12)\" stroke=\"#8b5cf6\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"180\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#8b5cf6\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"26\">one small word = liking the verb</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"222\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"24\">Ich trinke gern Kaffee. = I like drinking coffee.</text><rect x=\"60\" y=\"310\" width=\"980\" height=\"170\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"rgba(99,102,241,0.15)\" stroke=\"#6366f1\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"110\" y=\"375\" fill=\"#6366f1\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"28\">gern</text><text x=\"110\" y=\"425\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"24\">Ich trinke gern Kaffee.</text><text x=\"940\" y=\"405\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"20\">I like it</text><rect x=\"60\" y=\"510\" width=\"980\" height=\"170\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"rgba(245,158,11,0.15)\" stroke=\"#f59e0b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"110\" y=\"575\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"28\">lieber</text><text x=\"110\" y=\"625\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"24\">Ich trinke lieber Tee.</text><text x=\"940\" y=\"605\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"20\">I prefer it</text><rect x=\"60\" y=\"710\" width=\"980\" height=\"170\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"rgba(16,185,129,0.15)\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"110\" y=\"775\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"28\">am liebsten</text><text x=\"110\" y=\"825\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"24\">Ich trinke am liebsten Wasser.</text><text x=\"940\" y=\"805\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"20\">most of all</text><rect x=\"60\" y=\"930\" width=\"980\" height=\"90\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"rgba(255,215,0,0.1)\" stroke=\"#ffd700\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"987\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-size=\"24\">Same sentence, climbing word: gern, lieber, am liebsten</text></svg>",
      "caption": "Gern has no English twin: it sits beside a verb and means you like doing it, then climbs irregularly through lieber to am liebsten."
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "quiz",
     "question": "Ich trinke gern Kaffee, aber ich trinke ___ Tee. (You like coffee, but you prefer tea.) Which word fits the gap?",
     "options": [
      {
       "text": "lieber",
       "correct": true
      },
      {
       "text": "gerner",
       "correct": false
      },
      {
       "text": "besser",
       "correct": false
      },
      {
       "text": "am liebsten",
       "correct": false
      }
     ],
     "explanation": "Gern compares irregularly: gern → lieber → am liebsten. 'Lieber' is the preference step, exactly what 'aber' sets up here. 'Gerner' does not exist, 'besser' belongs to gut (good → better), and 'am liebsten' is the top step — what you like most of all, which would clash with singling out tea over just coffee.",
     "visual": {
      "type": "diagram",
      "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" class=\"lesson-visual\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"55\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"36\">WHICH STEP OF THE LADDER?</text><rect x=\"100\" y=\"150\" width=\"900\" height=\"200\" rx=\"16\" fill=\"rgba(99,102,241,0.12)\" stroke=\"#6366f1\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"230\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#6366f1\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"28\">Ich trinke gern Kaffee, ...</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"290\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"22\">step one is already taken</text><rect x=\"100\" y=\"420\" width=\"900\" height=\"200\" rx=\"16\" fill=\"rgba(245,158,11,0.12)\" stroke=\"#f59e0b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"500\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"28\">... aber ich trinke ___ Tee.</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"560\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"22\">aber signals: tea beats coffee</text><path d=\"M 550 350 L 550 420\" stroke=\"#ffd700\" stroke-width=\"4\" fill=\"none\"/><path d=\"M 538 405 L 550 425 L 562 405 Z\" fill=\"#ffd700\"/><rect x=\"100\" y=\"700\" width=\"900\" height=\"280\" rx=\"16\" fill=\"rgba(16,185,129,0.1)\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"765\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"26\">THE THREE RUNGS</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"825\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"24\">like it - prefer it - like it most</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"885\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"22\">one of these words is the middle rung</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"935\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"22\">and one of them does not exist at all</text></svg>",
      "caption": "The sentence climbs from liking coffee to preferring tea — the gap asks for the middle rung of the gern ladder."
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "concept",
     "title": "Compound Words: Read Right to Left",
     "content": "Time to pay the debt from lesson 3. German glues nouns together into single words — and there is one rule that unlocks all of them:\n\n**The LAST noun decides everything.** It sets the meaning (the word is a kind of that last thing) and the gender. So you decode from the right, walking left.\n\n• **die Haustür** = Haus + Tür — the house door. **Die**, because Tür is die.\n• **der Handschuh** = Hand + Schuh — a shoe... for your hand. A glove! **Der**, because Schuh is der.\n• **das Wörterbuch** (VOER-ter-bookh) = Wörter + Buch — a words-book. A dictionary.\n• **der Kühlschrank** (KUEL-shrahnk) = kühl + Schrank — a cool-cupboard. The fridge.\n• **das Krankenhaus** = kranken + Haus — the sick-house. A hospital.\n• **der Staubsauger** (SHTOWP-zow-ger) = Staub + Sauger — the dust-sucker. A vacuum cleaner.\n• **die Glühbirne** (GLUE-beer-nuh) = glüh + Birne — the glow-pear. A lightbulb — look at one and admit the shape is a pear.\n\nOnce you see it, German vocabulary starts feeling less like memorising and more like Lego.\n\nOne small detail for your reading eye: German sometimes drops a **linking letter** between the pieces — an **-s-**, **-n-**, or **-e-** that just smooths the joint. **Arbeit-s-zimmer** (workroom, study), **Straße-n-bahn** (street-railway: a tram). You never need to produce these; just recognise them so they do not throw off your decoding.",
     "visual": {
      "type": "diagram",
      "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" class=\"lesson-visual\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"55\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"36\">THE LAST NOUN RULES</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"112\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"22\">read right to left: gender colors from the LAST piece</text><rect x=\"60\" y=\"145\" width=\"480\" height=\"130\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"rgba(236,72,153,0.12)\" stroke=\"#ec4899\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"300\" y=\"200\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ec4899\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"26\">die Haustuer</text><text x=\"300\" y=\"245\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">Haus + Tuer = house door</text><rect x=\"560\" y=\"145\" width=\"480\" height=\"130\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"rgba(59,130,246,0.12)\" stroke=\"#3b82f6\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"800\" y=\"200\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#3b82f6\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"26\">der Handschuh</text><text x=\"800\" y=\"245\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">Hand + Schuh = a glove!</text><rect x=\"60\" y=\"300\" width=\"480\" height=\"130\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"rgba(16,185,129,0.12)\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"300\" y=\"355\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"26\">das Woerterbuch</text><text x=\"300\" y=\"400\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">Woerter + Buch = dictionary</text><rect x=\"560\" y=\"300\" width=\"480\" height=\"130\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"rgba(59,130,246,0.12)\" stroke=\"#3b82f6\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"800\" y=\"355\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#3b82f6\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"26\">der Kuehlschrank</text><text x=\"800\" y=\"400\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">cool + cupboard = fridge</text><rect x=\"60\" y=\"455\" width=\"480\" height=\"130\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"rgba(16,185,129,0.12)\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"300\" y=\"510\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"26\">das Krankenhaus</text><text x=\"300\" y=\"555\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">sick + house = hospital</text><rect x=\"560\" y=\"455\" width=\"480\" height=\"130\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"rgba(59,130,246,0.12)\" stroke=\"#3b82f6\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"800\" y=\"510\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#3b82f6\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"26\">der Staubsauger</text><text x=\"800\" y=\"555\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">dust + sucker = vacuum</text><rect x=\"60\" y=\"610\" width=\"980\" height=\"130\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"rgba(236,72,153,0.12)\" stroke=\"#ec4899\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"665\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ec4899\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"26\">die Gluehbirne</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"710\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">glow + pear = a lightbulb (look at the shape)</text><rect x=\"60\" y=\"790\" width=\"980\" height=\"220\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"rgba(245,158,11,0.12)\" stroke=\"#f59e0b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"848\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"26\">LINKING LETTERS: -s- / -n- / -e-</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"900\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"24\">Arbeit + s + zimmer = study</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"945\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"24\">Strasse + n + bahn = tram</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"988\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"20\">recognise them; never let them break your decode</text></svg>",
      "caption": "Seven compounds decoded right to left — the last noun sets both meaning and gender, and little linking letters like -s- and -n- just smooth the joints."
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "quiz",
     "question": "You see der Handschuh on a shop sign. It combines Hand and Schuh (shoe). What does it mean — and why is it der?",
     "options": [
      {
       "text": "A handshake — der because Hand decides the gender",
       "correct": false
      },
      {
       "text": "A shoe rack — der because Schuh decides the meaning",
       "correct": false
      },
      {
       "text": "A glove — der because Schuh, the last noun, decides the gender",
       "correct": true
      },
      {
       "text": "A glove — der because Hand, the first noun, decides the gender",
       "correct": false
      }
     ],
     "explanation": "Decode right to left: the word is a kind of Schuh (shoe), one specialised for the Hand — a glove. And the last noun rules the grammar too: Schuh is der, so Handschuh is der. Hand is actually die Hand — if the first noun decided, the word would be die.",
     "visual": {
      "type": "diagram",
      "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" class=\"lesson-visual\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"55\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"36\">DECODE: HAND + SCHUH</text><rect x=\"100\" y=\"180\" width=\"400\" height=\"220\" rx=\"16\" fill=\"rgba(139,92,246,0.15)\" stroke=\"#8b5cf6\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"300\" y=\"270\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#8b5cf6\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"32\">Hand</text><text x=\"300\" y=\"340\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"22\">the specialiser</text><rect x=\"600\" y=\"180\" width=\"400\" height=\"220\" rx=\"16\" fill=\"rgba(59,130,246,0.15)\" stroke=\"#3b82f6\" stroke-width=\"4\"/><text x=\"800\" y=\"270\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#3b82f6\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"32\">Schuh</text><text x=\"800\" y=\"340\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"22\">the boss: kind + gender</text><path d=\"M 760 460 L 340 460\" stroke=\"#ffd700\" stroke-width=\"4\" fill=\"none\"/><path d=\"M 355 448 L 335 460 L 355 472 Z\" fill=\"#ffd700\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"435\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-size=\"22\">read this way</text><rect x=\"100\" y=\"540\" width=\"900\" height=\"200\" rx=\"16\" fill=\"rgba(16,185,129,0.1)\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"615\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"28\">a Schuh ... for the Hand</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"675\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"24\">what do you wear on a hand like a shoe?</text><rect x=\"100\" y=\"800\" width=\"900\" height=\"200\" rx=\"16\" fill=\"rgba(245,158,11,0.12)\" stroke=\"#f59e0b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"870\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"26\">GENDER CHECK</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"930\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"24\">the LAST noun hands the whole word its article</text></svg>",
      "caption": "The decode runs right to left: Schuh is the boss noun, so the word is a kind of shoe — and Schuh's article, der, becomes the whole word's article."
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "application",
     "title": "The Monster, and Your Turn",
     "content": "First, the payoff. Here is a real German word you will hold in your hand at any doctor's office:\n\n**die Krankenversicherungskarte** (KRAHN-ken-fair-ZISH-er-oongs-kar-tuh)\n\nTwenty-five letters. Decode it right to left:\n\n• **Karte** — card. The last noun: this thing is a card, and Karte is **die**, so the whole word is die.\n• **Versicherung** — insurance (with a linking **-s-** smoothing the joint)\n• **Kranken** — sick\n\nA sick-insurance-card: a health insurance card. The monster was three friendly words in a trench coat.\n\nNow your turn — say these out loud, then build your own:\n\n**Six descriptions** with the no-ending pattern: **Der Kaffee ist kalt. Die Straße ist lang. Das Hotel ist teuer. Die Musik ist laut. Der Film ist traurig. Das Fenster ist offen.** Then describe six things in your own room.\n\n**Two comparisons** — one of each frame: **Der Zug ist schneller als der Bus.** **Mein Bruder ist so groß wie mein Vater.** Now compare two things you own.\n\n**Three compounds** from real labels and signs — decode each right to left before you peek: **das Schlafzimmer** (sleep + room), **die Sonnenbrille** (sun + **-n-** + glasses), **der Hauptbahnhof** (main + railway + station — a compound inside a compound). From today on, every long German word is an invitation, not a wall.",
     "visual": {
      "type": "diagram",
      "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" class=\"lesson-visual\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"55\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"36\">THE MONSTER, DECODED</text><rect x=\"60\" y=\"110\" width=\"980\" height=\"100\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"rgba(139,92,246,0.15)\" stroke=\"#8b5cf6\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"172\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"30\">die Krankenversicherungskarte</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"255\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"22\">walk it right to left</text><rect x=\"620\" y=\"290\" width=\"420\" height=\"140\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"rgba(236,72,153,0.15)\" stroke=\"#ec4899\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"830\" y=\"345\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ec4899\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"28\">3. Karte</text><text x=\"830\" y=\"395\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">card - die, so DIE wins</text><rect x=\"340\" y=\"460\" width=\"420\" height=\"140\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"rgba(99,102,241,0.15)\" stroke=\"#6366f1\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"515\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#6366f1\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"26\">2. Versicherung + s</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"565\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">insurance, linking -s-</text><rect x=\"60\" y=\"630\" width=\"420\" height=\"140\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"rgba(16,185,129,0.15)\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"270\" y=\"685\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"28\">1. Kranken</text><text x=\"270\" y=\"735\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">sick</text><path d=\"M 620 360 L 550 460\" stroke=\"#ffd700\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\"/><path d=\"M 340 530 L 270 630\" stroke=\"#ffd700\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\"/><rect x=\"560\" y=\"640\" width=\"480\" height=\"130\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"rgba(255,215,0,0.1)\" stroke=\"#ffd700\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"800\" y=\"695\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"24\">= health insurance card</text><text x=\"800\" y=\"740\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"20\">three words in a trench coat</text><rect x=\"60\" y=\"820\" width=\"980\" height=\"200\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"rgba(245,158,11,0.12)\" stroke=\"#f59e0b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"875\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"26\">YOUR TURN</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"922\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">6 descriptions with ist - 2 comparisons (als / wie)</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"965\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">3 compounds: Schlafzimmer, Sonnenbrille, Hauptbahnhof</text></svg>",
      "caption": "The 25-letter monster falls apart right to left into card, insurance, and sick — then the practice set: six descriptions, two comparisons, three decodes."
     }
    }
