     "explanation": "Besuchen takes a direct object — you visit SOMEBODY — and der Bruder is masculine, so mein shifts to meinen, exactly like ein became einen in lesson 5. Bare mein would only be right in the nominative (Das ist mein Bruder), and meine belongs to feminine and plural nouns. Bonus: Am Samstag fills position one, so besuche ich flips — verb second, as always.",
