     "explanation": "Regular participles are ge- + stem + -t, and because the stem arbeit- ends in -t, a helping -e- keeps the ending audible: gearbeitet. \"Gestern habe ich den ganzen Tag gearbeitet\" — I worked all day yesterday.",
     "visual": {
      "type": "diagram",
      "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" class=\"lesson-visual\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"55\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"36\">BUILD THE PARTICIPLE</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"160\" width=\"940\" height=\"150\" rx=\"16\" fill=\"rgba(99,102,241,0.15)\" stroke=\"#6366f1\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"225\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"28\">Gestern habe ich den ganzen Tag ____.</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"275\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"22\">(I worked all day yesterday.)</text><rect x=\"200\" y=\"380\" width=\"700\" height=\"140\" rx=\"16\" fill=\"rgba(255,215,0,0.1)\" stroke=\"#ffd700\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"440\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"32\">ge  +  ?  +  ?</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"490\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"22\">apply the recipe to the verb arbeiten</text><rect x=\"150\" y=\"590\" width=\"800\" height=\"130\" rx=\"16\" fill=\"rgba(139,92,246,0.12)\" stroke=\"#8b5cf6\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"645\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#8b5cf6\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"26\">Watch the stem: arbeit-</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"692\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">What does it end in? Does that change anything?</text><rect x=\"150\" y=\"790\" width=\"800\" height=\"160\" rx=\"16\" fill=\"rgba(16,185,129,0.12)\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"850\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"26\">Remember the bracket</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"900\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">habe sits in position 2 - the participle</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"935\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">closes the sentence at the end.</text></svg>",
      "caption": "Apply the ge- + stem + -t recipe to arbeiten, whose stem ends in -t."
     }
